  "argument": "The data provenance and methodological custody of this study are severely compromised, preventing independent verification. First, the study violates basic held-out discipline by executing a post-hoc analysis of 'Condition 2 on the raw path' that was never pre-registered, frozen, or predicted. Second, the spatial range calculations are based on an unnamed subset of storms, making it impossible for external researchers to audit or reproduce the aggregate results. Third, the raw data inputs lack rigorous quality control, as evidenced by the unvalidated inclusion of physically meaningless values (such as a 0.00 km catalogue radius and entirely missing feature frames) in the denominator. This combination of post-hoc metric adjusting and undocumented data-filtering choices invalidates the pipeline's integrity.",
  "dissent": true,
  "verdict": "unsupported"
}

